SET description='<p>Worker completed an unannounced home visit with the family. Worker asked Ms. Graves to speak outside of the hotel room. Worker explained that due to previous concerns discussed: Ms. Graves not engaging in mental health therapy, allowing various individuals to live in the home with her children causing them to be evicted, previous injuries sustained by Colby, allowing L. Ritter around the children unsupervised despite the Departments recommendation for him not to be, and now their current living situation which may not be sustainable, Ms. Graves needs to make a plan for her children. Ms. Graves became upset and began yelling at worker that she is a good mother, this worker does not understand how difficult it is struggling to raise two children on her own, Ms. Rosemary Graves is the one who brought individuals into their home, she was not aware of previous injuries or that Mr. Ritter was around Colby and Emmy unsupervised. Worker de-escalated the situation by empathizing with Ms. Graves. Ms. Graves identified her mother- Rosemary Graves to care for Emmy and Wendi Ritter to care for Colby. Worker contact Ms. Ritter to ask her to come to the hotel and pick up Colby. Ms. Graves contact Ms. Rosemary Graves to pick up Emmy.</p><p><br></p><p>Ms. Jenna Baldwin and Mr. Charles Sanner arrived with Emmy and Colby to the hotel room. Ms. Baldwin asked this worker if they could be considered a resource for Emmy. Worker expressed that she has the understanding that a registered sex offender is in the home- James Thompson. Worker would not recommend them as a resource due to that reason and Emmy having no ability to self protect. Ms. Baldwin explained that an incident occurred and he will be out of the home shortly. Worker obtained Ms. Baldwin''s household information to run background clearances to be considered a resource, per her request. Mr. Charles Sanner informed worker that he was charged with rape in the 80''s. He is a previous drug user, clean for 27years. An incident occurred where he beat up another individual because he owed him money. A few days later that mans girlfriend confronted him and Mr. Sanner beat her up, then she later pressed rape charges against him. She was 19 years old at the time and he was around 24 years old. He continues to be on parole as he was just released from jail last year. He completes numerous drug screens for his parole and for work at Chesapeake Ship Builders. He is not a registered sex offender.</p><p>Jenna Baldwin 10/23/84 11 West Chestnut St Delmar, MD 302-466-7070</p><p>Charles Sanner 8/4/60</p><p>Melody Rambo 1/28/59</p><p>Amiee Baldwin 3/27/05</p><p>Mackenzie Badwin 10/31/06</p><p>Payton Collins 3/20/12</p><p><br></p><p>Worker spoke with Ms. Rosemary Graves who agreed to care for Emmy. Ms. Rosemary Graves is currently residing at 911 Race Rd Cambridge, MD. In her household is Wayne Lednum 2/24/62. They rent the top half of the house and then there are three individuals living on the bottom half of the home related to Mr. Lednum. Worker completed a MD Case Search on Mr. Lednum prior to Ms. Graves leaving with Emmy. No criminal charges since 1983. Cleared on Md Sex Offender Registry.</p><p><br></p><p>Worker spoke with Ms. Wendi Ritter 9/11/84 who agreed to care for Colby. Ms. Ritter is living at 28588 Seaford Rd Laurel, DE 19956. Currently in her household is Sandra Herbert, Tina Ritter, and Jessee Hollie. No criminal charges found for residents in Maryland. Cleared on MD &amp; DE Sex Offender Registry.</p><p><br></p><p>Worker will complete a FIM referral.</p><p><br></p><p>Colby and Emmy appeared safe during the visit.</p>'
